\name{cellucid_cells_export}
\alias{cellucid_cells_export}
\title{Export the highlighted cells}
\usage{
cellucid_cells_export(viewer, format = "csv", page)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{format}{csv: the obs-column CSV; h5ad: an AnnData file of the highlighted cells. One of \code{"csv"}, \code{"h5ad"}. Default \code{"csv"}, the viewer's own.}
\item{page}{The highlight page; the page shown when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{bytes}, \code{cells} (Cells highlighted on it), \code{file} (The file written), \code{format}, \code{page} (The highlight page exported), \code{renamed} (Names an .h5ad cannot hold as they are, written under other names).
}
\description{
Write the highlighted cells of a highlight page as a file, as the Highlights list's export buttons do: an obs-column CSV (every open cell, a true/false column per highlight, which cellucid.pull() in Python and cellucid_pull() in R read back) or an .h5ad subset of the highlighted cells with their expression rows. The .h5ad reads the cells' expression first; its time and bytes are estimated from this connection before it starts.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{cells.export} (Exports). It acts outside the viewer's state and history (a file the person receives in the browser, a publication, or what the browser keeps for later visits), which Undo does not take back: it makes no step of the history.

When an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it, the viewer asks the person first (writes-file); from R it is not asked.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_cells_export(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
